# Build context for Dockerfile.vercel.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` copies the entire working directory into the
# image, which means two failures at once:
#
#  1. `.env` — with real API keys — is baked into a layer and pushed to the
#     container registry. A `.gitignore` does not stop this: Docker does not
#     read it.
#  2. The local `vendor/` directory, built with dev dependencies, overwrites the
#     `--no-dev` vendor from the composer stage. Package discovery then tries to
#     register a dev-only service provider that the production install does not
#     have, and the build fails on a class that is genuinely absent.

# Secrets and local configuration. `.env.example` stays, since it documents the
# variables without carrying any value.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed in their own stages, or not at all in the image.
vendor
node_modules

# Build outputs. The assets stage produces these fresh.
public/build
public/hot

# Runtime state. Never belongs in an image: it would ship one developer's
# database and log files to production.
storage/framework/cache/*
storage/framework/sessions/*
storage/framework/views/*
storage/framework/testing/*
storage/logs/*
database/*.sqlite
database/*.sqlite-journal

# Caches that would otherwise be read back instead of regenerated.
bootstrap/cache/*.php

# Version control and agent tooling.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.agents
.claude/skills
.cursor
.mcp.json
opencode.json
boost.json
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Deployment and documentation that the image does not need.
.vercel
.vercelignore
README.md